WEBVTT

c0
00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:05.179
Hey, Bert, come on out and meet
all these nice people, please.

c1
00:00:05.679 --> 00:00:08.340
All right, we really can't blame you.

c2
00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:11.720
You see, Bert is a very,
very careful fellow.

c3
00:00:12.039 --> 00:00:15.500
When there's danger, this is the
way he keeps from being hurt.

c4
00:00:16.319 --> 00:00:18.780
Sometimes it even saves his life.

c5
00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:21.926
That's why these children
are practicing to

c6
00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:24.989
duck and cover just as
you do in your school.

c7
00:00:25.829 --> 00:00:28.780
We all know the atomic
bomb is very dangerous.

c8
00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:32.150
Since it may be used against
us, we must get ready for it,

c9
00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:36.369
just as we are ready for many other
dangers that are around us all the time.

c10
00:00:36.869 --> 00:00:38.209
Fire is a danger.

c11
00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:41.779
It can burn whole buildings
if someone is careless,

c12
00:00:42.189 --> 00:00:43.900
but we are ready for fires.

c13
00:00:44.169 --> 00:00:47.130
We have a fine fire department
to put out the fire,

c14
00:00:47.389 --> 00:00:50.810
and you have fire drills in your
school, so you know what to do.

c15
00:00:51.669 --> 00:00:53.590
Automobile can be dangerous too.

c16
00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:56.990
They sometimes cause bad
accidents, but we are ready.

c17
00:00:57.270 --> 00:01:01.029
We have safety rules that car drivers
and people who are walking must obey.

c18
00:01:01.889 --> 00:01:06.209
Now we must be ready for a
new danger, the atomic bomb.

c19
00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:11.080
First, you have to know what happens
when an atomic bomb explodes.

c20
00:01:11.510 --> 00:01:12.989
You will know when it comes.

c21
00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:15.610
We hope it never comes,
but we must get ready.

c22
00:01:15.989 --> 00:01:19.910
It looks something like this. There is
a bright flash, brighter than the sun,

c23
00:01:20.019 --> 00:01:22.020
brighter than anything you've ever seen.

c24
00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:25.599
If you were not ready and
did not know what to do,

c25
00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:28.120
it could hurt you in different ways.

c26
00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:32.720
It could knock you down hard or
throw you against a tree or a wall.

c27
00:01:33.089 --> 00:01:36.485
It is such a big explosion,
it can smash in buildings and

c28
00:01:36.569 --> 00:01:39.919
knock signboards over and
break windows all over town.

c29
00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:44.779
But if you duck and cover like
dirt, you will be much safer.

c30
00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:47.739
You know how bad sunburn can feel.

c31
00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:52.309
The atomic bomb flash could burn
you worse than a terrible sunburn,

c32
00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.601
especially where you're not covered.

c33
00:01:54.839 --> 00:01:58.400
Now you and I don't have shells to
crawl into like Bert the turtle,

c34
00:01:58.550 --> 00:02:01.139
so we have to cover up in our own way.

c35
00:02:01.639 --> 00:02:06.496
First you duck, and then
you cover, and very tightly

c36
00:02:06.580 --> 00:02:08.979
you cover the back of
your neck and your face.

c37
00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:14.320
Duck and cover underneath a table
or desk or anything else close by.

c38
00:02:15.199 --> 00:02:18.720
In Betty's school, they are
talking about the atomic bomb too.

c39
00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:23.960
Betty is asking her teacher, how can we
tell when the atomic bomb may explode?

c40
00:02:24.115 --> 00:02:26.466
And her teacher is explaining
that there are two

c41
00:02:26.550 --> 00:02:30.190
kinds of attack with warning
and without any warning.

c42
00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:35.000
We think that most of the time we will
be warned before the bomb explodes,

c43
00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:38.000
so there will be time for
us to get into our homes,

c44
00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:40.259
schools, or some other safe place.

c45
00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:44.865
Our civil defense workers and our
men in uniform will do everything

c46
00:02:44.949 --> 00:02:49.330
they can to warn us before enemy
planes can bring a bomb near us.

c47
00:02:50.380 --> 00:02:53.800
You may be in your schoolyard
playing when the signal comes.

c48
00:02:57.179 --> 00:02:59.535
That signal means to stop whatever you are

c49
00:02:59.619 --> 00:03:02.639
doing and get to the
nearest safe place fast.

c50
00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:07.990
Always remember, the flash of an
atomic bomb can come at any time,

c51
00:03:08.199 --> 00:03:09.550
no matter where you may be.

c52
00:03:10.529 --> 00:03:13.329
You might be out playing at
home when the warning comes.

c53
00:03:15.679 --> 00:03:18.630
Then be sure to get into the house fast,

c54
00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:21.731
where your parents have fixed
a safe place for you to go.

c55
00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:25.380
If you are not close to home
when you hear the warning,

c56
00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:27.160
go to the nearest safe cover.

c57
00:03:27.929 --> 00:03:31.850
Know where you are to go or ask
an older person to help you.

c58
00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:34.860
You know the places
marked with the S sign.

c59
00:03:35.350 --> 00:03:38.229
They're safe places to go
when you hear the alarm.

c60
00:03:39.089 --> 00:03:43.070
If there is a warning, you will
hear it before the bomb explodes,

c61
00:03:43.490 --> 00:03:47.410
but sometimes, and this
is very, very important,

c62
00:03:48.089 --> 00:03:51.610
sometimes the bomb might
explode without any warning.

c63
00:03:52.484 --> 00:03:55.585
Then the first thing we would
know about it would be the flash,

c64
00:03:55.669 --> 00:03:58.690
and that means duck and
cover fast wherever you are.

c65
00:03:58.869 --> 00:04:00.889
There's no time to look around or wait.

c66
00:04:01.229 --> 00:04:05.529
Be like Bert. When there is a flash,
duck and cover and do it fast.

c67
00:04:06.839 --> 00:04:09.395
Here are some older boys
showing what to do if

c68
00:04:09.479 --> 00:04:11.979
the flash comes when you
are not in the classroom.

c69
00:04:12.289 --> 00:04:14.990
This is what to do if you
should be in a corridor.

c70
00:04:15.570 --> 00:04:18.769
You duck and cover tight
against the wall this way.

c71
00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:23.359
Remember to keep your face and the
back of your neck covered tightly.

c72
00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:27.290
Try to fall away from windows
or doors with glass in them.

c73
00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:31.220
Then if the glass breaks and flies
through the air, it won't cut you.

c74
00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:34.800
You might be eating your
lunch when the flash comes.

c75
00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:37.140
Duck and cover under the table.

c76
00:04:37.519 --> 00:04:40.470
Then if the explosion makes
anything in the room fall down,

c77
00:04:40.649 --> 00:04:41.959
it can't fall on you.

c78
00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:47.559
Getting ready means we will all have
to be able to take care of ourselves.

c79
00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:50.771
The bomb might explode when
there are no grown-ups near.

c80
00:04:51.519 --> 00:04:55.700
Paul and Patty know this, and they're
always ready to take care of themselves.

c81
00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:59.591
Here they are on their way to
school on a beautiful spring day,

c82
00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:01.961
but no matter where they
go or what they do,

c83
00:05:02.230 --> 00:05:07.119
they always try to remember what to do
if the atom bomb explodes right then.

c84
00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:09.700
It's a bomb, duck and cover.

c85
00:05:10.649 --> 00:05:12.429
Paul and Patty know what to do.

c86
00:05:12.995 --> 00:05:16.146
Paul covered the back of his head
so that he wouldn't be burned,

c87
00:05:16.230 --> 00:05:19.081
and Patty covered herself with
the coat she was carrying.

c88
00:05:19.739 --> 00:05:21.859
They knew how to duck and cover.

c89
00:05:22.059 --> 00:05:24.160
They acted right away when the flash came.

c90
00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:27.850
If they had been at this
doorway when the bomb flashed,

c91
00:05:27.950 --> 00:05:31.570
Paul and Patty would have ducked and
covered this way, like this girl.

c92
00:05:32.369 --> 00:05:34.869
Heavy doorways are a good
place to duck and cover.

c93
00:05:35.290 --> 00:05:36.649
She will be safer too.

c94
00:05:38.010 --> 00:05:40.489
Here's Tony going to
his Cub Scout meeting.

c95
00:05:40.890 --> 00:05:43.540
Tony knows the bomb can
explode any time of the year,

c96
00:05:43.649 --> 00:05:45.649
day or night, he is ready for it.

c97
00:05:46.170 --> 00:05:51.739
Duck and cover. Atta boy, Tony,
that flash means act fast.

c98
00:05:52.359 --> 00:05:55.009
Tony knows that it helps to
get to any kind of cover.

c99
00:05:55.320 --> 00:05:58.940
This wall was close by, so that's
where he ducked and covered.

c100
00:05:59.279 --> 00:06:00.619
Tony knew what to do.

c101
00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:04.141
Notice how he keeps from moving
or from getting up and running.

c102
00:06:04.329 --> 00:06:07.440
He stays down until he is
sure the danger is over.

c103
00:06:08.549 --> 00:06:11.519
The man helping Tony is
a civil defense worker.

c104
00:06:11.880 --> 00:06:16.070
His job is to help protect us when
there is danger of the atomic bomb.

c105
00:06:16.519 --> 00:06:18.839
We must obey the civil defense worker.

c106
00:06:20.070 --> 00:06:22.676
We must know how to duck and cover in the

c107
00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:25.619
school bus or in any
other bus or streetcar.

c108
00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:27.850
Duck and cover.
